(i) “Member of the family” is defined as:  
(1) (i) any person who is defined by or recognised under the law governing the benefits as a member of the family;  
(ii) for kind benefits under Title III, Chapter 1 (sickness, maternity, and equivalent paternity benefits), any person defined or recognised as a member of the family by the laws of the Member State where the person resides;  

(2) If the applicable Member State’s legislation does not distinguish between “members of the family” and other eligible persons, the spouse, minor children, and dependents who have reached the age of majority shall be treated as members of the family.  

(3) If, under the applicable legislation in paragraphs (1) and (2), a person qualifies as a member of the family or the household only by living in the same household as the insured or pensioner, this condition is met if that person is mainly dependent on the insured or pensioner.

